.TH PY-SLOWDOWN 1 "" "py-slowdown 2.0.0" "py-slowdown"
.SH NAME
py\-slowdown \- play audio slower or faster without changing its pitch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B py\-slowdown
[\-\-version] [FILE]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Play audio slower or faster without changing its pitch, with a waveform and bookmarks.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B FILE
an audio or video file to open, its .slx, or a file of Transcribe! (.xsc)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help and quit
.TP
.B \-\-version
show the version and quit
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Space
Play, or pause and go back to where it started
.TP
.B Shift+Space
Continue from the last pause
.TP
.B S
Stop and go back to the start
.TP
.B Home / End
Go to the start / to the end
.TP
.B ← / →
Back / forward (skip length)
.TP
.B Shift+← / Shift+→
Back / forward one second
.TP
.B ↓ / ↑ − / +
Slower / faster
.TP
.B N
Normal speed
.TP
.B Ctrl+↑ / Ctrl+↓
A semitone higher / lower
.TP
.B Shift+N
Original pitch
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+N
Reset the sound
.TP
.B B
Add a bookmark
.TP
.B Ctrl+← / Ctrl+→ PgUp / PgDn
Previous / next bookmark
.TP
.B Ctrl++ / Ctrl+− / Ctrl+0
Zoom in / out / whole file
.TP
.B Z
Zoom to the selection
.TP
.B Ctrl+wheel
Zoom around the pointer
.TP
.B L
Repeat the selection
.TP
.B Drag
Select with the mouse
.TP
.B I / O
Start / end of the selection at the position
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the selection
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
Select the whole file
.TP
.B Shift+L
Save the selection as a loop
.TP
.B C
Count in before playing
.TP
.B T
Tap the tempo (with the beat)
.TP
.B Shift+C
The first beat is here (count\-in)
.TP
.B K
Find the note of the selection
.TP
.B P
Track the pitch of the selection
.TP
.B R
Reference tone on / off
.TP
.B [ / ]
Reference tone a semitone lower / higher
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open a file
.TP
.B Ctrl+W
Close the file (the program stays open)
.TP
.B Alt+F4 Ctrl+Q
Quit
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save the .slx
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
Export the audio
.TP
.B Settings > Keyboard shortcuts
Change the shortcuts
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/py\-slowdown/py\-slowdown.conf
The settings: the window, the volume, the skip length, the language and the recent files.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/py\-slowdown/bookmarks.json
The bookmarks of each audio file, and the point where it was left ($XDG_DATA_HOME).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/py\-slowdown/
The decoded samples of the file open, in an unnamed temporary file that goes with it.
.SH AUTHOR
Nicolas Vaughan <nicolasvaughan@proton.me>
